    "result_text": "Tests green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI agreed with both findings and fixed them together:\n\n**Finding 1 (duplicated daily-count logic)** \u2014 Extracted the per-business-day owner count into a shared `BusinessDays.countCreatedOn(ownerRepository, businessDay)` helper. This is the natural home: `BusinessDays` is already the documented \"single source of truth\" for the effective registration date, so the count derived from that same concept belongs beside it. Both `EnsureDailyLimit` and `AssessBulkSignup` now call it; only their thresholds (100 vs 80) differ, so the two counts can no longer silently drift.\n\n**Finding 2 (inconsistent source of the business day)** \u2014 `AssessBulkSignup` now derives its day via `BusinessDays.effectiveRegistrationDate(owner.getRegistrationDate())`, the same routing `EnsureDailyLimit` uses, instead of reading `owner.getRegistrationDate()` raw. The call is idempotent (the stored date is already a rolled business day), so behaviour is unchanged, but the \"effective business day\" concept stays owned by `BusinessDays` rather than leaking out as an implicit dependence on `BuildOwner`'s ordering.\n\nNo acceptance behaviour changed \u2014 the pipeline wiring, the persisted `bulkSignupWarning` field, the schema, and the OpenAPI contract are all as before. The suite still passes.",
